course: dictionary
lesson: 4050
title: Generally: usually, and in most cases
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «generally» tells you that something is true most of the time, but not always. «Buddhists generally see him as a teacher, not as a god.» The sentence does not say every Buddhist thinks this. It says most of them do, so generally means usually.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. Words like «most», «many» and «usually» nearby often point to the same meaning. Try swapping in «usually» or «in most cases». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Generally can also mean by most people, or in a broad way without details. «It is generally believed» means many people think it is true. «Generally speaking» means you are describing the big picture and skipping the small details.
fact: «Generally» is an adverb, and it tells you how often or how widely something is true.
fact: «Generally» means usually, in most cases.
fact: «Generally» can mean by most people, widely known or accepted, as in «It is generally believed».
fact: «Generally speaking» means in a broad way, without going into details.
fact: Scientists often write «generally» because there can be exceptions, for example «Plants generally need light».
exercise: «Plants generally need light to grow.» What does generally mean here? | Quickly and loudly | *Usually, in most cases | Never, not at all | Only once
exercise: «It is generally believed that the story is true.» What does generally mean here? | Hardly anyone | Angrily | Secretly, by one person | *By most people, widely
exercise: What does the phrase «generally speaking» mean? | Speaking to a crowd | In a loud voice | *In a broad way, without details | In a very careful way, with every detail
test: Scientists write «Generally, plants need light» instead of «Plants always need light». Why? | To make the sentence longer | *Because there can be exceptions | Because plants are never wrong | To show the plants are happy
test: In «Buddhists generally see him as a teacher, not as a god», which meaning fits best? | Only one Buddhist | *Most Buddhists, in most cases | Nobody at all | Every single Buddhist, without exception
exam: Which word means the same as generally in «Dogs are generally friendly»? | Rarely | *Usually | Never | Always
